  "@type": "sc:Dataset",
  "conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.0",
  "name": "MUVIS-DIR",
  "description": "MUVIS-DIR is a deep-imbalanced-regression (DIR) evaluation benchmark built on the published MuViS multimodal virtual-sensing suite (Brandt et al.). It is NOT a new dataset: it reuses MuViS's unified preprocessing and predefined train/test splits for nine multimodal time-series extrinsic-regression tasks drawn from six independently published, openly licensed source datasets, and adds a DIR-specific evaluation protocol (task selection, a seed-dependent 90/10 train/val split, Freedman-Diaconis balanced bins, and the bMAE / bMASE balanced metrics). Each distributed split is an sktime .ts file with inputs X of shape (N, T, D) and target y of shape (N,). Underlying source datasets are referenced by persistent identifier in `isBasedOn` and in the per-task `source_doi` / `source_license` fields; they retain their original licenses. The MuViS preprocessing and this evaluation layer (code, task/split/bin definitions, metrics) are released under the MIT License. IMPORTANT: the redistributed source data is under MIXED licenses (CC-BY-4.0, CC0-1.0, BSD-3-Clause, ODC-By-1.0) and, for the Tire Temp. task (Vehicle Dynamics Dataset), the copyleft CC-BY-SA-4.0 license, whose ShareAlike term applies to redistributed derivatives of that task. Consult the per-task `source_license` field before redistributing any individual split.",
  "conformsToProtocol": "DIR evaluation (bMAE/bMASE)",
  "url": "https://anonymous.4open.science/r/MUVIS-DIR",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "license": "Mixed: MUVIS-DIR evaluation layer and MuViS preprocessing under MIT (https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT.html); redistributed source data under the per-task licenses in recordSet 'tasks' (source_license) — CC-BY-4.0, CC0-1.0, BSD-3-Clause, ODC-By-1.0, and CC-BY-SA-4.0 (Tire Temp.).",
  "citeAs": "Anonymous. Exposing Blind Spots in Deep Imbalanced Regression Evaluation. Under review, NeurIPS 2026. Built on MuViS (Brandt et al.).",
